  "description": "Aggregate the work that delivers this outcome: command exit codes and the list-envelope count each have one owning test.\n\n## Background\n\nThis story groups the test-topology tasks that share one design surface, so they can be reviewed together once each has landed.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [hard] REQ-01: Command-to-exit-code bindings and their human/machine parity are proven only by the exit-code projection suite, which fails for a projected row without a binding case. Other subprocess tests assert only what they add.\n- [hard] REQ-02: The list-envelope `count` property is proven by one test that covers each list-emitting command, and no per-command test re-asserts it.\n",
